ull, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 419340, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013TRnpzVd9fYxZeBw1rmwue", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 422699, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016bZVTyuq3EVDVaJEKNxbo2", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 422999, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016bZVTyuq3EVDVaJEKNxbo2", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 422999, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016bZVTyuq3EVDVaJEKNxbo2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 427929, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, which fixes CVE-2026-31337. CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The vulnerability:** a high-severity flaw where parsing deeply nested arrays can cause unbounded recursion. It's fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I picked 2.9.4 because it's the smallest fixed version that keeps you on 2.x, so no major-version upgrade.\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`. It changes the fastjson pin in `requirements.txt` and adds a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (a7ffe29fb7).\n- **The PR:** the request to open it timed out. When I checked, PR #101 had been created anyway but had no reviewer, so I added alex rather than opening a second PR.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking up the advisory an