nt": [{"citations": null, "text": "The PR (#101) was created, but alex isn't on it as a reviewer yet. I'll add him.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016bZVTyuq3EVDVaJEKNxbo2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, which fixes CVE-2026-31337. CI passed, and PR #101 against main is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The vulnerability:** a high-severity flaw where parsing deeply nested arrays can cause unbounded recursion. It's fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I picked 2.9.4 because it's the smallest fixed version that keeps you on 2.x, so no major-version upgrade.\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`. It changes the fastjson pin in `requirements.txt` and adds a security entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (a7ffe29fb7).\n- **The PR:** the request to open it timed out. When I checked, PR #101 had been created anyway but had no reviewer, so I added alex rather than opening a second PR.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}